G2_INSTANTON|tag=MEASURED+NAMED|chirality=ASD|orientation=C oriented by psi on C = vol_A complement orientation (measured equal)|text=On R7 = A x C (A associative, C coassociative) a connection pulled back from C, invariant under translations of A, has curvature F in Lambda2 C tensor g at every point. If F is anti-self-dual on C (measured: Lambda2_- C lies in Lambda2_14 and has F^psi = 0), then pi_7(F) = 0, the G2-instanton equation (Donaldson-Thomas 1998, Gauge theory in higher dimensions). Example: the BPST instanton (Belavin-Polyakov-Schwarz-Tyupkin 1975) pulled back to R3 x R4 is a G2-instanton with energy density constant along R3.|json=0
